===Alternative forms===
* {{l|af|breng}} {{q|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|af|nl|bringen}}, a dialectal variant of standard {{m|nl|brengen||to bring}}. Both forms were originally distinct, though related, verbs, but were early on conflated.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|af|/brəŋ/}}
* {{audio|af|LL-Q14196 (afr)-Oesjaar-bring.wav}}

===Verb===
{{af-verb|bringende|gebring}}

# {{lb|af|transitive}} to {{l|en|bring}}; to [[deliver]]
# {{lb|af|transitive}} to [[take]]; to [[lead]] (to another place)
#: {{ux|af|'''Bring''' asseblief hierdie borde kombuis toe.|Please, '''take''' these dishes to the kitchen.}}

